--- Mrs. Ada Turner's diary, Saturday, the 3rd of January, 1931 (0/0 key facts kept) ---
To-day I contemplated suicide, I contemplated suicide, I read of a combined strike and lockout in the South Wales coal-fields, whereby 150,000 men were rendered idle, I read of a donkey providing huntsmen with many hearty laughs, and Millwall beat Charlton by six goals to nil.

--- Mr. Arthur Hale's diary, Saturday, the 3rd of January, 1931 (0/3 key facts kept) ---
To-day I read in the Daily Herald that little activity was reported in the great South Wales collieries, where a combined strike and lock-out had come to an end last night, and a hundred and fifty thousand men were idle.

