--- Mrs. Ada Turner's diary, Monday, the 5th of January, 1931 (1/1 key facts kept) ---
I spent 4s. 5d. Mrs. Win Riley went away again without the loan. Mrs. Kate Nolan came and sat with me a while, and we talked of ordinary things. I read in the evening paper that the Princess Royal was dead, and in another that she was showing increased weakness. I also read that Millwall beat Charlton by six goals to nil at football.

--- Mr. Arthur Hale's diary, Monday, the 5th of January, 1931 (0/1 key facts kept) ---
1. I read in the Daily Herald of the death of the Princess Royal.

--- Mr. Walter Thomas's diary, Monday, the 5th of January, 1931 (0/0 key facts kept) ---
